course: dictionary
lesson: 14808
title: Purify: making things clean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To purify something means to make it clean and pure, so that dirt, germs or harmful things are taken out. «The campers had to purify the river water before they drank it.» The water looked clear, but boiling it removed the germs. So purify means to make something clean and safe.
explain: The same word works for things that are not water. «The air purifier in our classroom cleans the air we breathe.» A purifier takes dust and dirt out of the air. Ask yourself: what is being removed? That tells you what purify means.
explain: People also use purify for feelings and hearts. «She prayed each morning to purify her heart.» Here purify means to make someone feel spiritually clean, free from guilt. The word can be about water, air or a person, and the meaning is always about taking out what is bad.
fact: Purify means to make something pure by removing dirt, germs or harmful things.
fact: «Purify water» means to clean water so it is safe to drink, for example by boiling or filtering it.
fact: In science, you can purify a substance by separating it from a mixture.
fact: «Purify the air» means to clean the air, often with a machine indoors.
fact: Purify is a verb: purify, purifies, purified, purifying.
exercise: «Boil the water to purify it.» What does purify mean here? | *To make it clean and safe by removing germs | To make it louder | To colour it blue | To make it colder
exercise: «The air purifier cleans the air in the room.» What is an air purifier for? | *To remove dirt and dust from the air | To make the room darker | To play music | To make cakes
exercise: «She prayed to purify her heart.» Find and copy the word that tells you what she wanted to make clean. | prayed | heart | *purify | she
test: Mum says, «We will purify the water with a filter.» What does purify mean? | To pour it on the plants | *To clean it by removing dirt and germs | To colour it | To freeze it solid
test: Which sentence uses purify to mean making someone spiritually clean? | He asked the shop to purify the bread | The painter will purify the wall | *He asked God to purify his heart | The bus will purify the street
exam: Which word means nearly the same as purify? | Mix | Spoil | Hide | *Clean
